hat receives the request later than this after the session service stored it does nothing.")}).describe("@internal A replacement worker asks the attached client that serves this session's tools to announce it, when a call names a machine its roster lacks. Not addressed to an instance: the worker knows none. A client that serves the machine announces, overriding once what it believes the worker already holds; it honours one ask per epoch, another only when the announce that one made failed or went unanswered, and at most one per ten seconds, and does nothing for an ask it cannot date or read, or whose sender it would refuse a tool call from. Any other client, and a client that predates the request, does nothing or error-replies, and the worker reads no reply: it withdraws the request with control_cancel_request when its wait ends.")),TVe=f(()=>u({subtype:T("turn_handoff"),messages:C(Fe([un(),pn()])).min(1).max(200).describe("@internal The turn so far, in conversation order: the user's message, any [assistant, tool_result] rounds already answered elsewhere, and last an assistant message (thinking blocks with their signatures, text, and the tool_use blocks to run). Every message carries a uuid, kept as the transcript line's; none of the messages, and none of the tool_use ids they hold, may already be in the conversation \u2014 the turn is appended once, whole, never merged with lines already there (except as tool_use_ids describes for a turn that runs nothing). No two assistant messages share a message id, among these or with the conversation, with one exception, for a worker whose turn_handoff entry has shared_message_id: an assistant message that holds tool_use blocks only may repeat the id of the assistant message before it where every message between them, at least one, holds only tool_result blocks for that earlier message's calls. The two are then sent to the model as one message, its calls followed by their results, so a client does this only for calls of one Messages API response that it ran one after another. A request that names calls to run is refused (invalid_handoff) unless its first message is a user message, not empty and not a tool_result."),tool_use_ids:C(o()).max(16).describe("@internal The tool_use blocks of the last message to run, each of a tool named in the turn_handoff entry of the worker external_metadata; all run in one batch, then the model continues once. May be empty, and then nothing runs and no model turn follows: with every call the turn carries answered within it (the last message holding none), the worker appends the turn as history and, once the lines are stored, echoes the last assistant message that holds a call; with stopped, the user stopped the turn before its calls ran. In both cases, when a leading part of the turn is already in the conversation from an earlier delivery, only the rest is appended; where its first assistant message repeats the id of the last one already there, as messages allows, the two are sent to the model as one message."),stopped:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Only true, and only with an empty tool_use_ids: the user stopped this turn while its last message, an assistant message holding calls that have not run, was being handed over. The worker appends the turn, closes those calls and marks the turn exactly as when a turn of its own is stopped before a call runs, and ends it with the result a stopped turn ends with; when an earlier delivery already appended the turn, the calls are closed in place."),relay_marker:u({type:T("system"),subtype:T("upgrade_relay_marker"),uuid:o(),content:o()}).optional().describe("@internal The system line that starts the prompt-cache relay for this conversation: uuid is the line's uuid, and content is the marker, a JSON string whose anchor_line_uuid is the uuid of the first of messages; other fields of the line are ignored. Only a worker that advertises relay_marker: true in turn_handoff_available uses it, on a request that names calls to run, or on a history request (no calls named, not stopped) if the session holds none of its messages yet. It is never a reason to refuse the turn: when the member is not such a line, or the worker does not use the marker, the request is answered as without it."),memory_context:u({uuid:o(),version:o().nullable(),content:o().nullable()}).optional().describe("@internal The snapshot of the user's claude.ai memory that the client showed its model with the turn's user message. Used on a request that names calls to run, or on a history request (no calls named, not stopped) if the session holds none of its messages yet: the worker writes it ahead of the first of messages, with uuid as the line's uuid, as a cowork_memory_context attachment line like those it writes for snapshots it fetches itself, and then adds no copy of that version. version and content are both strings for a snapshot, both null to withdraw an earlier one. The member is never a reason to refuse the request: one that is malformed, that has a version without content or the reverse, or whose uuid is also that of one of messages, of relay_marker or of a line the session's transcript holds, is ignored, and the turn goes on without the line."),message_client_platform:o().optional().describe("@internal The `anthropic-client-platform` value of the app a person sent the first of messages from. Left out when no person sent that message, as in a scheduled run. When it names one of the Remote Control apps (isRemoteControlAppPlatform) and that message is not one from another session, the worker marks the message as sent by a person, as it marks a user message that arrives with that value, so the turn counts as started by a person for the calls it runs and for those the model makes afterwards, and the turn the worker runs carries that value as its client platform, as a turn for such a user message does (per-turn telemetry, and tools that read which app the person is on). The member is never a reason to refuse the request: without it, or with any other value, the message is appended unmarked and the turn carries no platform."),file_names:C(u({file_uuid:o(),name:o()})).max(16).optional().describe("@internal Files a person attached to the conversation, each with the name the client showed its model for it, the most wanted first; at most 16. file_uuid is that of a file_attachments entry on a user message sent to this worker before the request. Only a worker that advertises file_names: true in turn_handoff_available uses the member, only on a request that names calls to run, and only when those calls run in the session's home directory: before they run, it copies each listed file it has downloaded into that directory, under that name, until a limit on time or on total size is reached, taking first the names that occur in the calls' own input. It replaces nothing then, skips a name it refuses or that the list holds twice, and, within one request, skips the further names of a file once it has found or placed one of them. If a person later sends another file under a name it placed, it puts that file's bytes in the copy's place, or removes the copy if it cannot, and only while the copy is still the file it placed, unchanged. The member is never a reason to refuse the request: a malformed one (a longer list included) is ignored whole, and the calls run whatever became of the copies.")}).describe('@internal Sent by the session client to a worker that advertises turn_handoff in its external_metadata: hand over a turn whose final assistant message holds tool calls that have not run. The worker answers at once \u2014 success {status: "accepted"} (validated and queued; the messages are appended at the start of the turn that runs the calls, the last one echoed back as an assistant event before any call runs; a request that runs nothing (see tool_use_ids) for the same turn as one still queued to run replaces it), success {status: "duplicate"} (every named call is already taken by an earlier delivery or answered; nothing runs \u2014 taken, not necessarily ran; or, for a turn that runs nothing, its calls are already answered by other lines, or the same turn is already pending in that shape or running), or an error whose message starts with its code and a colon: turn_handoff_disabled, invalid_handoff, unsupported_tool, unknown_tool, recovered_by_restart (this worker restarted after the turn was appended and its recovery set the turn\'s unrun calls aside; this request will not run or close them), expired (the request names calls to run and the session service has held it for over 30 minutes, by the created_at of the frame that delivered it: the service hands a request that no worker answered to every later worker of the session; nothing is appended or taken, and a request that runs nothing is never refused for its age). Accepted calls get the permission evaluation of the worker (rules, the permission mode, can_use_tool to the client); their tool_result messages and the model continuation follow on the event stream as in any turn.')),qY=f(()=>u({status:B(["accepted","duplicate"]),tool_use_ids:C(o()).optional().describe("@internal The calls queued to run (status accepted).")}).describe("@internal Success payload answering turn_handoff.")),ua=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_message"),server_name:o(),message:tR()}).describe("Carries one MCP JSON-RPC message for an SDK-hosted MCP server (one named in initialize.sdkMcpServers or added later with mcp_set_servers). Flows in both directions: the CLI sends it to the client to reach the in-process server, and the client sends it to the CLI to deliver that server's own messages. When the client answers, the success response carries the server's JSON-RPC reply under mcp_response; the CLI acknowledges a client-sent one with an empty success.")),GY=f(()=>u({mcp_response:tR().optional().describe("The JSON-RPC response the SDK-hosted server produced for the delivered message (for a JSON-RPC notification, a response with an empty result). Present when the client answers a CLI-sent mcp_message; absent when the CLI acknowledges a client-sent one.")}).describe("Success payload answering an mcp_message request.")),pa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_set_servers"),servers:me(o(),cn())}).describe("Replaces the set of dynamically managed MCP servers.")),BY=f(()=>u({added:C(o()),removed:C(o()),errors:me(o(),o())}).describe("Result of replacing the set of dynamically managed MCP servers.")),ma=f(()=>u({subtype:T("reload_plugins"),hold_on_cache_impact:O().optional().describe("When true, the reload is not applied if applying it would change the session's tool list while the conversation's prompt cache depends on that list (the same check the interactive /reload-plugins makes before it asks for --force): the response then carries held: true and cache_impact, and the session keeps its current plugins. Default false: apply unconditionally."),add_plugins:C(snt()).optional().describe("Plugins for the reload to load as well, in the same shape as the SDK `plugins` option: each entry joins the session as one more --plugin-dir would (--plugin-dir-no-mcp when skipMcpDiscovery is set). Plugins already loaded stay; nothing is removed. A held or failed reload adds none of them. Refused for a malformed list or a path that is not absolute, when managed settings set disableSideloadFlags, on a connection whose frames persist server-side (any Remote Control or cloud worker), in a cloud-hosted session, and when a running sandbox cannot keep shell commands out of the folders (always on Windows).")}).describe("Reloads plugins from disk and returns the refreshed session components.")),KY=f(()=>u({commands:C(Wt()),agents:C(lo()),plugins:C(u({name:o(),path:o(),source:o().optional(),version:o().optional().describe(mo)})),mcpServers:C(io()),error_count:E().int(),held:O().optional().describe("Present only when the request asked to hold on cache impact and this CLI ran the check. True: the reload was not applied, the lists above describe the session as it still is, and cache_impact says what applying would change. False: the check found no impact and the reload was applied. Absent: the request did not ask, or the CLI predates the option and applied the reload unchecked."),cache_impact:u({mcp_servers_added:C(o()),mcp_servers_removed:C(o()),lsp_tool_change:B(["adds","may-add","removes","may-remove"]).nullable()}).optional().describe("What applying the held reload would change in the session's tool list: plugin MCP servers it would register or drop (scoped plugin:<plugin>:<server> names, plugin-authored \u2014 validate before showing) and whether it would add or remove the LSP tool (the may- forms mean the preview could not fully see the pending plugin set). Present only with held: true.")}).describe("Refreshed commands, agents, plugins, and MCP server status after reload.")),_a=f(()=>u({subtype:T("reload_skills")}).describe("Reloads skills from disk and returns the refreshed skill list.")),HY=f(()=>u({skills:C(Wt())}).describe("Refreshed skill commands after reload.")),ga=f(()=>u({subtype:T("reload_output_styles")}).describe("Re-reads the output-style directories from disk (a style file written mid-session is otherwise invisible until the next session) and returns the refreshed style names. Also drops the shared markdown-file scan cache, so agents, skills and routines re-read their directories on their next use.")),FY=f(()=>u({available_output_styles:C(o())}).describe("Refreshed output style names after reload, built-in and custom, in the order the initialize response lists them.")),fa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("register_repo_root"),directory:o(),reload_claude_md:O().optional(),reload_plugins:O().optional(),reload_skills:O().optional()}).describe("Add a directory as a working-directory root and optionally reload CLAUDE.md, skills, and plugins. The directory must resolve to a strict subdirectory of cwd, or of a directory passed at launch via --add-dir / the SDK additionalDirectories option. A directory that is already a registered working directory (including a duplicate of an earlier request) is denied with an error; the registration pipeline and DirectoryAdded hooks do not re-run.")),WY=f(()=>u({directory:o().describe("The registered root. A resolved absolute path \u2014 except on connections that persist frames server-side (the local bridge-worker lane echoes the request directory verbatim; the registration is still keyed on the resolved path locally).")}).describe("Success payload answering register_repo_root.")),ba=f(()=>u({subtype:T("set_cwd"),path:o().describe("Target directory. Tilde-expanded and realpath-canonicalized by the CLI, exactly like an interactive /cd argument."),trust_accepted:O().optional().describe("Host attestation that the user explicitly accepted a trust dialog for this directory. Only send true after showing one \u2014 the CLI records the directory as trusted (the same latch /cd's own prompt writes) before relocating. Requires trusted_directory."),trusted_directory:o().optional().describe("Required whenever trust_accepted is true: the exact directory string from the needs_trust response being answered. This pins the attestation to the canonical path the user was shown \u2014 if the raw path canonicalizes differently by the time the re-send arrives (e.g. a symlink component changed during the dialog), nothing is latched and a fresh needs_trust carries the new canonical directory.")}).describe("@internal Moves the session to a new working directory \u2014 the headless twin of /cd, for SDK hosts like Claude Desktop. Runs the same validation, Cd(...) permission rules, and relocation path as the interactive command, with the trust prompt delegated to the host via the needs_trust response arm. Before the first turn the move re-anchors start-of-session state (the first request is built as for a start in the new directory, no move notice); after a turn the prefix is preserved and the move arrives as an appended notice. SessionStart hooks are never re-run by set_cwd (those of the launch directory already ran and their output stays in the session); a host that starts the process before its directory is known should use --await-claim and claim_session, which run them in the bound directory instead. Rejected while a turn is in flight.")),YY=f(()=>Kr("status",[u({status:T("ok"),cwd:o().describe("Canonical (realpath) working directory the session now runs in."),changed:O().describe("False when the target already was the working directory \u2014 a successful no-op with no side effects."),transcript_relocated:O().describe("True when the transcript lives in the project slot derived from cwd (the normal case, and the no-op case). False only on the documented edge where the move completed but the transcript move failed AND the rollback chdir failed \u2014 a cwd-derived resume lookup will then miss the session.")}),u({status:T("needs_trust"),trust_root:o().optional().describe("Present when `directory` sits inside a git repository whose canonical root differs from it (a subdirectory or a linked worktree). Accepting trust grants that whole repository \u2014 every subdirectory and linked worktree of the root \u2014 so the trust dialog should name this root alongside `directory`. Informational only: the attestation echo still pins `trusted_directory` to `directory`. Vetted by the same visible-glyph rule as `directory`; a canonical root that fails it is omitted rather than carried."),directory:o().describe("Canonical target directory. Nothing changed; show a trust dialog for exactly this string and, on accept, re-send with trust_accepted: true and trusted_directory echoing it verbatim. Safe to render verbatim in the dialog, by construction: every character is a visible, space-distinguishable glyph. Targets whose canonical path contains control (Cc), format (Cf), default-ignorable, line/paragraph-separator (Zl/Zp), non-ASCII-space Zs, or braille-blank code points are rejected (reason: unsafe_path) before this arm can carry them.")}),u({status:T("rejected"),reason:B(["not_found","not_a_directory","blocked_by_rule","busy","unsafe_path"]).describe("unsafe_path: the target's canonical path contains characters that do not render as visible, space-distinguishable glyphs \u2014 control (Cc), format (Cf), default-ignorable, line/paragraph-separator (Zl/Zp), non-ASCII-space Zs, or braille-blank code points; rejected fail-closed before the trust round-trip, and the offending path is never echoed back."),message:o().describe("Human-readable, ANSI-free explanation.")})]).describe("@internal Result of a set_cwd request. Every non-ok outcome leaves the working directory unchanged \u2014 but trust may already have been durably recorded when the request carried a valid attestation (a busy rejection or relocation failure after the latch does not unlatch it; the consent was for the directory, not the attempt). Internal failures (e.g. the transcript move failed and was rolled back) arrive as a control_response error instead.")),pnr=f(()=>u({subtype:T("claim_session"),cwd:o().describe("The session's working directory. Tilde-expanded and realpath-canonicalized; treated exactly like the cwd a process is spawned in (no trust prompt, no Cd(...) rule check) \u2014 the host chose it, as it chooses a spawn cwd."),env:me(o(),o()).optional().describe("Per-session environment additions. Only keys on the claim allow-list are accepted (keys the process has already consumed \u2014 config dir, base URL, proxy/TLS, provider, telemetry, entrypoint \u2014 must be part of the spare's spawn env); any other key rejects the claim and leaves the spare parked."),additional_directories:C(o()).optional().describe("Extra directories the session may access, as --add-dir."),permission_mode:o().optional().describe("Session permission mode, as --permission-mode. Part of the claim (not a follow-up set_permission_mode) so that a mode the process cannot take \u2014 bypassPermissions on a spare spawned without --allow-dangerously-skip-permissions, a mode this build does not know, one the claimed directory's settings disable \u2014 refuses or fails the claim instead of letting the first turn run under the spare's mode."),system_prompt:C(o()).optional().describe("As initialize.systemPrompt."),append_system_prompt:o().optional().describe("As initialize.appendSystemPrompt."),agents:me(o(),oe()).optional().describe("As initialize.agents."),title:o().optional().describe("As initialize.title."),sdk_mcp_servers:C(o()).optional().describe("The session's final set of in-process SDK MCP server names. Diffed against the set registered while parked: new names are connected, missing ones disconnected. Omitted: the parked set stays."),include_initialize:O().optional().describe("When true the ok response also carries the payload an initialize response would (commands, agents, models, account \u2026) computed for the claimed directory, for hosts that render them."),workspace_trust:u({accepted:O(),directory:o()}).optional().describe("As initialize.workspaceTrust, for a claimed spare: the host's attestation that the user accepted a trust dialog for the session's folder, judged against the claimed cwd once the spare has moved there, by the same rule (honored only from the process that owns the CLI's stdin, and only when `directory` resolves to that folder's trust key). A spare's own initialize arrives in its parking directory and records nothing, so a host that attests sends it here. workspace_trust_recorded in the response (and in the returned initialize payload) reports the outcome.")}).describe("@internal Binds a parked spare (a process started with --await-claim in a neutral directory with the host-level options) to its session: relocates it to cwd as if it had been spawned there, applies the per-session prompt options and in-process MCP server set, starts the SessionStart hooks, and registers the session. Model, thinking budget and flag-settings overlays are not claim fields: send set_model / set_max_thinking_tokens / apply_flag_settings right behind the claim; the control loop applies them in order before it reads the first message. A set_model that arrives before the first message is applied the way --model is at start-up: it writes no /model entries to the transcript and makes no extra API call to confirm a model id the local checks accept. Accepted once, only on a parked spare, only before any turn. A request that fails validation is refused before anything is touched and leaves the spare parked; a failure after that point leaves the spare unusable (discard it).")),$Y=f(()=>u({status:T("ok"),cwd:o().optional().describe("Canonical working directory the session now runs in (omitted when the canonical path carries invisible or non-printing characters, which are never echoed)."),session_id:o(),parked_ms:E().optional().describe("How long the spare was parked before this claim."),sdk_mcp_settled:O().describe("Whether the in-process SDK MCP handshakes registered while parked had completed when the claim arrived (false: the first turn still waits for them)."),initialize:me(o(),oe()).optional().describe("Present when include_initialize was true: the initialize-shaped payload for the claimed session."),workspace_trust_recorded:O().optional().describe("As initialize's workspace_trust_recorded: present when the claim came from the process that owns the CLI's stdin and carried workspace_trust with accepted true and an absolute directory; true when the claimed folder is now recorded as trusted (or already was), false when the attestation was not honored.")}).describe("@internal Result of a successful claim_session. Failures arrive as a control_response error whose message starts with a reason token (not_a_spare, already_claimed, busy, turn_started, env_key_not_claimable:<KEY>, cwd_not_found, cwd_not_a_directory, \u2026); the spare stays parked after any of them.")),Ea=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_reconnect"),serverName:o()}).describe("Reconnects a disconnected or failed MCP server.")),Sa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_toggle"),serverName:o(),enabled:O()}).describe("Enables or disables an MCP server.")),Ta=f(()=>u({subtype:T("mcp_read_resource"),serverName:o().describe("Server name, as mcp_status reports it (not normalized)."),uri:o().describe("The resource to read. Must use the ui:// scheme; any other URI is refused.")}).describe('Reads one MCP Apps (SEP-1865) UI resource \u2014 a `ui://` URI, typically the `_meta.ui.resourceUri` a tool declares \u2014 from a connected MCP server the CLI itself dialed, with `resources/read`, for a host that renders it. Read-only and no model turn. The reply is untrusted third-party content (HTML): render it sandboxed. SDK-type MCP servers (config.type === "sdk") are rejected \u2014 they are caller-provided, so the caller can read them directly. Errors name the cause: a non-ui:// URI, an unknown server, a server that managed policy blocks, that is disabled or that the project has not approved (the refusals mcp_reconnect gives), a server that is not connected (failed, pending or needs-auth: send mcp_reconnect; a connected server, or one still listed from the discovery cache, is read through the same connect path a tool call takes), a response over the size limit, or the server\'s own resources/read error. Refused on a lane that redacts what it persists (a Remote Control bridge worker, a tenant worker) and by the client of a cloud-hosted session. Advertised as `mcp_read_resource_v1` in system/init.capabilities.')),XY=f(()=>u({contents:C(u({uri:o(),mimeType:o().optional(),text:o().optional(),blob:o().optional().describe("Base64, for a binary item."),_meta:me(o(),oe()).optional().describe("The content item's own `_meta` as the server sent it (MCP Apps puts the resource's `ui.csp` and `ui.permissions` here), minus keys under the CLI-reserved `com.anthropic/` prefix.")}))}).describe("The server's resources/read result for an mcp_read_resource request.")),wa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("set_mcp_permission_mode_override"),serverName:o(),mode:de().nullable(),askForTools:C(u({name:o().regex(dwn)})).max(hVt).nullish().describe("@internal With mode 'default': tools of this server, named without the mcp__<server>__ prefix (a name sent with it is stored without it; the 64-character limit applies to the name as sent), that must ask even where the tool would otherwise allow itself (today only Claude in Chrome's safe permissionless tools, e.g. tabs_context_mcp). Held beside the pin: a clear, an 'auto' pin, or a pin sent without this member (or with null or an empty list) removes the list, silently. A list of the wrong shape is refused and changes nothing.")}).describe("@internal Pin (or clear, with mode:null) an MCP server's per-tool permission-mode override. Tighten-only over this channel: only 'default', 'auto', or null are accepted (clampControlChannelOverride); any other mode is rejected without changing state. The override substitutes for the session mode at every per-tool engine decision (effectiveModeForTool) \u2014 and only when the session mode would already auto-allow \u2014 so e.g. a server can be held at 'default' or routed through the auto-mode classifier under global bypassPermissions.")),JA=()=>o().regex(/^[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,64}$/),fnr=f(()=>u({subtype:T("set_chrome_browser_hints"),preferredDeviceId:JA().nullable().optional(),localDeviceIds:C(JA()).max(32),hostPlatform:B(["darwin","win32","linux"]).optional()}).describe("@internal The host's view of which Claude in Chrome browser this session should use when several are connected to the account: `preferredDeviceId` is the browser its user picked last on that computer, `localDeviceIds` the relay device ids it knows to be running on that computer right now, `hostPlatform` that computer's OS (for the weaker same-OS label). Session memory only, never persisted; the built-in claude-in-chrome server reads them as its persisted pick and its on-this-computer set, so it defaults to that browser instead of asking. Hints only: nothing is selected unless it is in the live relay roster, and an empty list clears them.")),mnr=f(()=>u({subtype:T("set_prompt_suggestions_paused"),paused:O()}).describe("@internal Pauses (true) or un-pauses (false) the session's prompt suggestions at runtime, for a host whose composer is not on screen: while paused, no turn end starts a suggestion, and the first turn end after paused is set back to false does. The state is one boolean in this CLI process, on top of the initialize request's promptSuggestions option and the user's own setting, neither of which it changes: a respawned or resumed session starts unpaused, so the host must send it again, and with two clients attached one client's pause applies to both. Acknowledged with an empty success; a CLI build where this is not yet enabled acknowledges and keeps generating, and an older CLI answers an unknown-subtype error.")),ya=f(()=>u({subtype:T("stop_task"),task_id:o()}).describe("Stops a running task.")),Aa=f(()=>u({subtype:T("background_tasks"),tool_use_id:o().optional().describe("When set, backgrounds only the task whose originating tool_use block has this id. When omitted, backgrounds all foreground tasks (Ctrl+B semantics).")}).describe('Backgrounds in-flight foreground tasks (Bash commands and subagents). With tool_use_id, targets the single task started by that tool_use block; without it, backgrounds all foreground tasks \u2014 the control-request equivalent of pressing Ctrl+B in the terminal. Each blocking tool call returns immediately with a "running in the background" tool_result and the turn continues; the task keeps running and emits a task_notification when it settles.')),QY=f(()=>u({backgrounded:O().optional().describe("Present only when the request named a tool_use_id: whether a matching foreground task was found and backgrounded. Empty object when all foreground tasks were backgrounded.")}).describe("Success payload answering background_tasks.")),Ra=f(()=>u({subtype:T("get_task_output"),task_id:o().describe("A shell or Monitor task of t